From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 02:53:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] zone: count only the fuel class, so a model that also
 detects robots does not count robots

zone passed every box the model returned to its tracker. With a three-class model (fuel,
robot_blue, robot_red) a robot box inside the ROI became a track and was counted as fuel.
On one frame of a 2026 Einstein broadcast, a three-class model gave 6 robot boxes in a
wide ROI.

zone now asks the model for the class named "fuel" when it has one (a classes: key
overrides it). A single-class model whose class has another name keeps counting every box,
as before. Tests: 26 pass (4 new, pure: no model).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
